Z||000003||Raydar||10-18-2000||09:30 AM||||Check this link...<BR> <A HREF="http://www.gmpowertrain.com/engines_marine/30_main.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.gmpowertrain.com/engines_marine/30_main.htm</A> <P>It doesn't have the crossflow head, and it looks like it has the standard Chevy bolt pattern for the trans mount. <BR>This is probably an evolution of the old 153 C.I. engine that used to come in early 60s Novas and maybe 70s Monzas. <BR>I am told that it is unrelated to the Iron Duck. (I used to believe differently.)<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 10-18-2000).]||||reg||1
